NAME
       tac - print lines in reverse order, last line first

SYNOPSIS
       tac [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       tac is cat backwards: it prints the lines of each file (or standard
       input) starting with the last one. Handy for log files, where the
       newest lines are at the end.

EXAMPLES
           tac /var/log/messages | head -20

SEE ALSO
       cat(1), tail(1), sort(1)
